{
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "text": "After FY2018 Apple switched from reporting revenue under the legacy 'Revenues' concept to the newer ASC 606 concept 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax', so the old concept appears to stop.",
      "how_to_test": "SELECT rf.fiscal_year, rf.fiscal_period, rf.concept, COUNT(*) AS fact_count
FROM edgar.revenue_facts rf
WHERE rf.cik = 320193
  AND rf.concept IN ('Revenues', 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax')
GROUP BY rf.fiscal_year, rf.fiscal_period, rf.concept
ORDER BY rf.fiscal_year, rf.fiscal_period;"
    },
    {
      "text": "The EDGAR ingestion pipeline missed or dropped Apple's 'Revenues' facts for filings after FY2018 due to a coverage gap (e.g., a temporary outage or filter misconfiguration).",
      "how_to_test": "SELECT rf.filed_date, rf.accession_number, rf.form_type
FROM edgar.revenue_facts rf
WHERE rf.cik = 320193
  AND rf.concept = 'Revenues'
  AND rf.filed_date > (SELECT MAX(filed_date) FROM edgar.revenue_facts WHERE cik = 320193 AND concept = 'Revenues' AND fiscal_year <= 2018)
ORDER BY rf.filed_date;
If this returns zero rows, it indicates missing data after FY2018."
    },
    {
      "text": "Later filings contain duplicate or overridden 'Revenues' facts with null/zero values that obscure the true revenue, making it appear as if reporting stopped.",
      "how_to_test": "SELECT rf.fiscal_year, rf.fiscal_period, rf.value_usd, rf.period_frame
FROM edgar.revenue_facts rf
WHERE rf.cik = 320193
  AND rf.concept = 'Revenues'
  AND rf.fiscal_year > 2018
ORDER BY rf.fiscal_year, rf.fiscal_period;
Check whether value_usd is NULL, 0, or unusually low compared to prior years."
    },
    {
      "text": "Apple adopted a new business segment reporting structure after FY2018, causing revenue to be reported only under subsidiary-specific concepts rather than the consolidated 'Revenues' concept.",
      "how_to_test": "SELECT rf.concept, COUNT(*) AS cnt
FROM edgar.revenue_facts rf
WHERE rf.cik = 320193
  AND rf.fiscal_year > 2018
GROUP BY rf.concept
ORDER BY cnt DESC;
If 'Revenues' disappears while other revenue-related concepts (e.g., 'ProductSales', 'ServiceSales') appear, this supports the hypothesis."
    }
  ]
}
